# Tailwind CSS v4

- **Utilities first:** Style with Tailwind utility classes in markup. Keep shared tokens and base styles in the existing CSS entry (Vite `@tailwindcss/vite`), not one-off CSS modules unless necessary.
- **Theme tokens:** Prefer semantic/theme colors and spacing already defined in the design system over hardcoded hex/rgb when a token exists.
- **DaisyUI:** Do not add DaisyUI (or other component CSS kits) unless explicitly requested.
- **Responsive:** Mobile-first breakpoints; avoid layout that only works at one viewport.
- **Focus styles:** Never strip focus outlines without a visible `focus-visible:` replacement (see WCAG rule).
